# Hive Engine

C++20 portfolio project: a work-stealing job system + archetype-based SoA ECS, a custom profiler, and a "Swarm" boids demo (raylib + ImGui). The full plan lives in `docs/hive-engine-plan.md`; follow its milestones (M1-M7) and don't build ahead of the current one.

## Principles
- Performance and clarity over cleverness. Every abstraction must justify its cost.
- Data-oriented design: think about memory layout and cache behavior first.
- No hidden allocations in hot paths (jobs, ECS iteration, per-frame code).
- Small, focused changes. Don't refactor unrelated code.
- Never claim something is faster without a benchmark measured in Release.

## Layout
- `core/` allocators, containers, math
- `jobs/` scheduler and work-stealing deques
- `ecs/` entities, archetypes, queries, systems
- `profiler/` scope macros, per-thread buffers, viewer
- `demo/` Swarm app
- `bench/` Google Benchmark
- `tests/` Catch2 tests
- `docs/` plan, design notes, performance investigation

## Build
- Configure/build with CMake presets: `cmake --preset debug`, `cmake --build --preset debug`.
- Toolchain is MSVC on Windows (Ninja generator); CI also builds on Linux with Clang/GCC.
- New source files must be added to the relevant `CMakeLists.txt`.